{
  "about": [
    "What the dashboard must show after the vendor responses in licor.json and wqdata.json go through ingestion.",
    "Ingestion runs three times (ingest.py): at 07:35Z, at 08:00Z, and at 08:00Z again, which must add nothing.",
    "The browser's clock is set to 08:00Z on 2026-11-01 (03:00 in Toronto), so the default date range is Oct 31 to Nov 1, in every browser time zone (17:00 Nov 1 in Tokyo, 08:00 in London).",
    "The download (every group ticked, the default days) must hold every row below, and be named for those two days.",
    "recorded_at in rows is Toronto wall-clock time, as the API and the download show it; recorded_at_utc is the instant the database stores. Clocks went back at 06:00Z (02:00 EDT -> 01:00 EST), so 01:00-01:59 happens twice: both copies are stored, as two instants with the same wall-clock time.",
    "The charts' 10-minute points are on real time, so each copy of the repeated hour is its own point. The download has one line per instant, in time order: the repeated hour's wall-clock times appear on two lines.",
    "Water Surface Elevation = z - L * cos(theta) + sensor depth, with Logger 1's z = 39.701, L = 1.525, theta = 57.7 degrees (utils/parsers.py), i.e. 38.88611266718051 + depth."
  ],
